  "findings": [
    "Current rare-query and CJK-body costs include avoidable semantic work and payload generation; a single global memory-bandwidth bottleneck description is unsupported.",
    "Native snapshot results establish substantial metadata opportunity, but broader prefixes retain 4096 candidate scoring and are slower than rare queries.",
    "Compact result movement helps some workloads, but a large apparent byte count alone does not identify the dominant stage.",
    "Threshold-two banded OSA passed differential checks yet produced no substantial end-to-end gain on the tested real queries.",
    "Larger SQLite cache increases dirty cached bytes with limited benefit; larger mmap may reduce pager copying but does not reduce the mapped resident working set to zero.",
    "Positional CJK retrieval and deferred offscreen excerpts jointly give a much smaller first-screen compute path, without removing visible snippets."
  ],
  "implementation_order": [
    "Version the body tokenizer, rebuild old body indexes safely, and validate positional matching before removing the current full-body validation.",
    "Split result identity/rank from display payload, generate visible excerpts on demand, retain generation checks and stable selection, and reuse progressive query state.",
    "Introduce a native metadata snapshot behind a guarded fallback; intern directory paths and string data, choose sparse/dense postings by cardinality, and persist a read-only snapshot plus bounded updates.",
    "Use the existing metadata database as the pending extraction spool; bound directory/content descriptor batches and builder memory independently of corpus size.",
    "Profile and then optimize remaining fuzzy candidate generation, normalization, index-update batching and IPC; evaluate additional SIMD or background parallelism on measured hotspots.",
    "Measure cold launch, actual input-to-display P99, filesystem stalls, writer/read concurrency, index rebuild peaks, long-lived memory and energy before declaring an app-level improvement."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Timings exclude Swift conversion, dispatch queues, path-existence checks, icon lookup, AppKit layout, GPU presentation and animation.",
    "Native snapshot memory numbers count retained C allocations; they exclude SQLite, allocation overhead, construction peak, old/new snapshot overlap, mapped resident pages and app footprint.",
    "The 100k synthetic data has regular ASCII names/paths; it is not representative of every user corpus.",
    "Native fast-path validation is not a proof for all inputs. Non-ASCII/multiword single-character cases require fallback or additional index support. Error, cancellation, snapshot lifetime, concurrent updates and truncation contracts remain integration work.",
    "The deferred-title result deliberately leaves offscreen snippets unmaterialized; its P50 is not the duration to populate every returned snippet.",
    "Hardware counters characterize one warm baseline query loop; they do not classify every query or the whole app.",
    "Changing mmap/page-cache settings has not been validated under memory pressure, index writes or cold storage.",
